[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Sprint Review: Stakeholder Feedback and Product Inspection in Scrum"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"The Sprint Review is a crucial Scrum event held at the end of a Sprint to inspect the Increment and adapt the Product Backlog if needed. It is not merely a status meeting, but a collaborative working session designed to showcase completed work and gather actionable stakeholder feedback."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Core Objectives of the Sprint Review"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Inspect the Increment: The Scrum Team presents the results of their work to key stakeholders."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Review Product Backlog: Discuss the current state of the Product Backlog in relation to market trends or stakeholder needs."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Collaborate on Next Steps: Collaborate on what to do next to optimize value creation in subsequent sprints."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Typical Sprint Review Agenda"},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"1. Welcome and Context Setting: The Product Owner welcomes participants and sets the stage by reviewing the Sprint Goal."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"2. Demonstration (Demo): Developers demonstrate the \'Done\' items completed during the Sprint."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"3. Feedback Collection: Stakeholders provide feedback, ask questions, and test usability."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"4. Product Backlog Adjustment: The Product Owner updates the Product Backlog based on the feedback received."},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Handling Stakeholder Feedback Effectively"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Not all feedback should immediately alter the product direction. The Product Owner is responsible for analyzing feedback against the product vision, budget, timeline, and overall strategy before adding new items to the Product Backlog."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"// Pseudo-code representing Product Owner decision logic for feedback
if (feedback.alignsWithVision && feedback.addsMeasurableValue) {
    ProductBacklog.addItem(feedback.translateToUserStory());
} else {
    ProductBacklog.archive(feedback);
}"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Success"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Show working software, not PowerPoint slides."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure all items demonstrated meet the strict Definition of Done."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep the meeting conversational and open rather than rigid and formal."}]
